          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 10 FAQ -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center;">10 / FAQ</p>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Agricultural Steel Buildings</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-faq">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can steel buildings be used for poultry and livestock farms?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. Steel structures are widely used for poultry houses, cattle barns, pig farms and other livestock facilities. Steel portal frames provide large-span, column-free interiors ideal for animal housing and equipment layout. With appropriate ventilation, insulation and corrosion-resistant surface treatment, steel buildings provide durable, cost-effective and fast-to-erect solutions for agricultural applications.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>How do you handle ventilation in livestock buildings?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Ventilation is handled through structural provisions in the steel building design, including ridge vents, eave openings, side wall inlets, exhaust fan openings and appropriate roof slopes. The specific ventilation strategy (natural, mechanical, tunnel or mixed) is determined based on animal type, building size, local climate and operational requirements. ZhongSai provides the structural framing and enclosure provisions for ventilation systems; mechanical ventilation equipment (fans, controllers) is supplied by specialized equipment manufacturers.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
